# Public configuration, committed on purpose.
#
# Every value here is PUBLISHABLE: Vite inlines anything prefixed `VITE_` into
# the JavaScript bundle, so these are readable by anyone who opens the site
# whether they live in this file or in a hosting dashboard. Committing them
# makes a fork or a second environment a configuration change rather than a
# code change.
#
# OpenFrame Tabletop has no backend yet. The hosts below end in `.invalid`, a
# name reserved so that it can never resolve, and stand in until the Tabletop
# Supabase project and rooms Worker exist (Phase 1). They are placeholders on
# purpose: the values this file used to hold named OpenFrame's own deployment,
# and a checkout of this repository must not be able to reach it.
# `app/detached.test.ts` fails the build if those names come back.
#
# What protects anything is a row-level security policy on the database and the
# room's own authorization — never a value in here. `app/env-file.test.ts`
# fails the build if anything that looks like a secret is added.

# The room server. Absent means this build does not collaborate.
VITE_COLLAB_URL=wss://rooms.unprovisioned.invalid

# Identity. Absent means this build has no accounts and every board is local.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://unprovisioned.invalid
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_unprovisioned
